#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:8
msgid "nvme-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `nvme-control` interface allows snaps to manage and access NVMe "
"controllers,alongside namespaces via in-kernel NVMe interfaces (PCI & NVMe-"
"oF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"This interface provides access to enumerate devices, create/delete/attach/"
"detach namespaces, and read device health/ telemetry data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"Access is limited to NVMe management operations through sysfs, nvme-fabrics "
"char device, and controller/namespace device nodes. Raw block I/O remains "
"constrained by device cgroups. The nvme and nvme-tcp kernel modules may auto-"
"load as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"For further details on interfaces, see {ref}`How to connect interfaces "
"<explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:18
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:20
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:29
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:31
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nvme-control-interface.md:24
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

